  "seconds_source": "Local Windows pytest JUnit testcase durations. Each pair used the same command and machine. Picotool, defmt, install eval and pyOCD used a four-worker selection at time scale 6. Loopback and source walk used a separate serial selection. Debugger process timings come from a serial selection of nine hang cases and include the Windows process-identity correction. Seconds sum only the measured cases within each module, including setup and teardown. Counts are from full module collection. OpenOCD readiness and debugger process-tree cases retain the startup time needed to record their transcripts and process identities. GDB interrupt cases retain their original acknowledgement allowance because the scaled lower cap increased the wait at factor 6. The CI target is 130 s saved per macOS leg, with about 90 s expected per Linux and Windows leg because the remaining cases retain real processes and deadlines.",
